% ============================================================================
% reference-line-hemisphere-split.query.adj — a worked recall over the
% geography reference-line-hemisphere-split library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "which hemispheres does
% the equator divide?": it states no geography fact of its own — it only
% `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves
% each `?` against the `reference_line_hemisphere_split` rows and returns
% the hemisphere split + the table's source/locator/trust. A reference line
% the cited spans give no hemisphere split for abstains honestly — the
% engine never invents one.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli reference-line-hemisphere-split.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "reference-line-hemisphere-split.adj"

? reference_line_hemisphere_split(equator, $Hemispheres)          % expect northern_southern
? reference_line_hemisphere_split($Line, eastern_western)         % reverse bind — expect prime_meridian
? reference_line_hemisphere_split(tropic_of_cancer, $Hemispheres) % expect abstain — the tropic's own cited span states a latitude limit, not a hemisphere split
